¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”In the same quarters were possessions of the chief man of the island, whose name was Publius; who received us, and lodged us three days courteously.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©And it came to pass, that the father of Publius lay sick of a fever and of a bloody flux: to whom Paul entered in, and prayed, and laid his hands on him, and healed him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\So when this was done, others also, which had diseases in the island, came, and were healed:¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
